-- title:
--   Annihilating U_q²-1 near θ' at a ramified prime
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{O}$ be a characteristic-zero discrete valuation domain, complete for the adic topology of its maximal ideal and with finite residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal{O}$, and let $p$ be a prime whose image in $\mathcal{O}$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$: a two-dimensional $k$-vector space $V$ together with a monoid homomorphism $\bar\rho.\rho$ from $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$ to $\mathrm{End}_k V$ that is trivial on the automorphisms fixing some finite-dimensional intermediate field, and assume its base change to $\overline{k}$ admits no invariant submodule other than $\bot$ and $\top$. Let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be finite sets of naturals with every member of $S$ prime and $p \in S$, and let $N \neq 0$ be such that every prime divisor of $N$ lies in $S$ and none lies in $S_0$; assume the weight-two level-$N$ integral structure hypothesis, that the $\mathbb{C}$-span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice generated by the cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ with integral $q$-expansion coefficients is everything. Let $\theta'$ be a ring homomorphism to $k$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S_0$, and $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$, $q \notin S_0$. Assume that for every prime $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ a non-unit in $P$, and every $\sigma$ in the decomposition subgroup of $P$ acting on the residue field of $P$ by $x \mapsto x^{\ell}$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho.\rho(\sigma)$ equals $X^2 - \theta'(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Finally let $q$ be a prime with $q \neq p$, $q \mid N$, $q^2 \nmid N$, at which $\bar\rho$ is ramified, in the sense that there is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $q$ is a non-unit and an element of its inertia subgroup over $\mathbb{Q}$ acting non-trivially. Then there exists $r$ in [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S₀`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) with $\theta'(r) \neq 0$ and $r \cdot (U_q^2 - 1) = 0$.
--
--   This is the Steinberg-prime input at a prime exactly dividing the level: at a prime $q \neq p$ with $q \| N$ where the residual representation is ramified, the element $U_q^2 - 1$ of the Hecke algebra is annihilated by something not in the kernel of the residual eigensystem $\theta'$, so that $U_q^2 = 1$ after localisation at the maximal ideal attached to $\theta'$. It is used in the proofs that the localised Hecke algebra is reduced and that $U_q^2$ becomes $1$ there.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_heckeAlgebra_exists_apply_ne_zero_and_mul_U_sq_sub_one_eq_zero_of_not_isUnramifiedAt.lean

